# Only the dashboard (public/) and the proxy (api/) belong on Vercel.
#
# The backend runs on its own server. If Vercel can see server.mjs or
# package.json it auto-detects a Node server project and tries to boot the
# backend as a function, which fails since VOUCH_API_KEY only exists on the
# real host. Hiding them makes this a plain static + functions deployment.
server.mjs
package.json
scripts/
.env.example
